"""Plain-English review of metric DEFINITIONS (the metric-page 'what this means' line) — 2026-08-10.

Reviewed all 333 active definitions (6-slice generate + per-slice accuracy verify vs
question + options). The field was in poor shape: 158 were verbatim copies of the
question, 33 were auto-generated boilerplate ('Binary indicator for whether...'), and
some described a different metric than the question. Replaced 308 with accurate,
one-sentence plain-English definitions that explain what the metric captures and how to
read the answer scale (distinct from the question, no invented facts, British spelling).
Text-only (definition column); options/type/values untouched. DB is the live source the
app serves (library.py -> the metric page 'Question & definition' card). LUMI_DB-aware;
DRY-RUN unless --write --confirmed-by-david.
"""
import os, sys, sqlite3

DB = os.environ.get("LUMI_DB") or os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "..", "lumi.db")
